        <item>
            <title>1.6</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:31:30 +0700</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.45 -apple-system,system-ui,sans-serif;margin:0;padding:0 4px}h2{font-size:20px;margin:6px 0 4px}h3{font-size:13px;margin:16px 0 4px}p{margin:4px 0}.date{opacity:.6}ul{margin:4px 0;padding-left:20px}li{margin:4px 0}code{font:12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace}</style></head><body><h2>1.6</h2><p class="date">Release date: 24 Sep 2026</p><h3>New in 1.6</h3><ul><li>See where your tokens actually go – switch the list between Skills, Agents and Tools. Each skill now counts only the tokens of its own turn, and the rest shows up as a separate No skill row.</li><li>Agents – every subagent type with its launches and tokens, next to the main session.</li><li>Tools – tokens split across Bash, Read, Edit and each MCP server.</li><li>Skills read directly from their SKILL.md now count as runs, and skills loaded at session start get their share of tokens.</li><li>Minor UX/UI improvements, including a floating panel that no longer slips under the menu bar.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
